## Why This Is Asked
Assess the candidate’s ability to structure a practical CBA for a distributed architecture shift, weighing latency, privacy, and cost against risk reduction and retention gains.

## Key Concepts
- Edge computing vs centralized analytics
- Inference costs, device storage, data transfer
- Regulatory/compliance penalties and risk
- Uplift in fraud detection and user retention
- Break-even analysis and sensitivity testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function breakEven(initialCost, monthlySavings, monthlyCosts) {
  let months = 0;
  let net = -initialCost;
  while (net < 0) {
    net += (monthlySavings - monthlyCosts);
    months++;
  }
  return months;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design the data governance model to satisfy privacy regulations across regions?
- What mitigation plans exist if edge devices underperform (false positives, latency spikes, battery impact)?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device crypto trade-offs for privacy-focused apps.

## Key Concepts
- On-device key management
- Key rotation cadence
- AES-256-GCM encryption
- Impact on battery, CPU, memory
- Privacy/compliance costs

## Code Example
```javascript
async function encryptNote(note, key) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const alg = { name: 'AES-GCM', iv };
  const ciphertext = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(alg, key, enc.encode(note));
  return { iv, ciphertext: new Uint8Array(ciphertext) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to measure encryption energy impact on mobile?
- How to rotate keys without re-encrypting all notes?

## Why This Is Asked

